🧠 How the Chatbot Works
1. Receive User Input

The chatbot asks the user to enter a message.

You: hello
2. Process the Input

The input is converted to lowercase so that the chatbot can compare it with predefined messages.

3. Select a Response

The program uses if-elif-else statements to determine the appropriate response.

4. Continue Conversation

A while loop keeps the chatbot running.

5. Exit

When the user enters:

bye

the chatbot says goodbye and terminates.

▶️ Demo
Example Conversation
================================
        BASIC CHATBOT
================================

Type 'bye' to exit the chatbot.

You: hello
Bot: Hi!

You: how are you
Bot: I'm fine, thanks!

You: what is your name
Bot: Sorry, I don't understand.

You: bye
Bot: Goodbye!

🚀 How to Run
Option 1 — Google Colab
Open the .ipynb notebook.
Open it in Google Colab.
Run the code.
Enter a message when prompted.
Type bye to end the conversation.
Option 2 — Local Python

Clone the repository:

git clone YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL

Navigate to the project:

cd CodeAlpha_Basic_Chatbot

Open the notebook using Jupyter Notebook or JupyterLab.

📓 Project Notebook

The complete implementation is available in:

CodeAlpha_Basic_Chatbot.ipynb

